[{"code":"prepend_in_loop","severity":"warning","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":10,"col":47},"end":{"line":10,"col":51}},"title":"PREPEND IN LOOP","message":"This puts elements in front of `acc`, the accumulator this `List.foldr` hands\nback to its callback, so it happens at every step:\n\n    [ x, …acc ]\n\nA list is an array, so every step copies the whole accumulator, and the loop\ntakes time that grows with the square of the list's length. Add at the end\ninstead, which takes the same short time at every step:\n\n    [ …acc, x ]\n\n`List.foldr` hands over the last element first, so to keep the order write\nthe loop as `List.foldl`, which hands over the first element first.\n\nIf the prepend is meant — the list stays short — give the new list a name\nfirst, and this warning goes."},{"code":"not_implemented","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":18,"col":13},"end":{"line":18,"col":14}},"title":"NOT IMPLEMENTED YET","message":"A limit of the compiler: `browser-inline` does not compile markup that is not\nwritten in place, or a branch whose arms are not one element and `<></>` yet\n(`docs/design/browser-inline.md` §5, class 1). Write the `view` without it, or\nbuild this program with `--platform=browser-tea`, which compiles it."}]
